 "title": "Graph Theory and Additive Combinatorics",
 "byline": "Yufei Zhao \u00b7 Cambridge University Press, 2023 (author\u2019s version)",
 "note": "Exercise lists inside chapters are not broken out. Summaries are in our own words; the text stays in the PDF.",
 "summary": "A graduate text built around the parallels between extremal graph theory and additive combinatorics, organized by the question of when dense structures must contain patterns like triangles or arithmetic progressions. It covers Tur\u00e1n-type problems, the regularity method and removal lemmas, pseudorandom graphs and spectral methods, graph limits (graphons), homomorphism inequalities, Fourier-analytic and polynomial proofs of Roth\u2019s theorem, Freiman\u2019s theorem on sets with small doubling, the sum-product problem, and the Green\u2013Tao theorem via the transference principle.",
